WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.271
Week 25: Future, Probability, and Forecasting. make forecasts state commitments express probability about the present

2
00:00:08.271 --> 00:00:15.540
Cultural lens. Public forecasts about demographics, environment, technology, and economic life.

3
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:27.974
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.974 --> 00:00:39.981
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.981 --> 00:00:49.194
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:49.194 --> 00:01:24.156
Model language. Los pronósticos sobre demografía cambian con el tiempo. — Forecasts about demographics change over time. El medio ambiente influye en la tecnología futura. — The environment influences future technology. La vida económica depende de muchos factores. — Economic life depends on many factors. Es importante separar evidencia de especulación. — It's important to separate evidence from speculation. Calibrar bien un pronóstico es difícil. — Calibrating a forecast well is difficult.

7
00:01:24.156 --> 00:01:34.310
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
